<description>&lt;p&gt;Algeria has sent troops to Niger for the first foreign mission in over 50 years to protect energy assets, while Nigerian forces repelled bandits in Niger, killing a soldier and prompting calls for more bases. A convoy of Governor Bago in Niger crashed, killing four students, a driver and a young lady. ISWAP leader responsible for attacks in Owo, Kogi and Niger was killed in Ondo. Niger has accused Chad of a drone strike that killed two civilians, and an overcrowded NSCDC detention cell in Niger caused the deaths of 14 minors among 33 detainees. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihAFBVV95cUxOSnI5SFhPUVdSMlJIV05qVkh6Qk8zblBnNWRnRGh0Y21QSGd4bDVxSEJjSDlGbG9YV3QtdTN3Q3NRTFlIZUdEX0dFLTNmTkswOHY2Q1BaUzZDekEza2pFalFkdDgwMDRvQzJOSHB4UUg4YWk4TEFoSGNBTnBvaWF1ZEtma28?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijgFBVV95cUxQVWRlbGthWTRRT3JhYm1teDk4dWpTTk9LX2hOT1ZZWU81RUt1N3FVQXJtU1pFZEY4ZmhCTzVLWnNVaVlhUllreWxwaDlqRmhzSVg3bVNCMElRa3JwX3puTUtiWU9CVmhmRjRlZlJDX0FlVDAxNk9qVDY2ejBWZnUtWkt6X0lQbEd6cUxLUHRB?oc=5&quot;&gt;Real Broadcasting Network&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMigwFBVV95cUxOTVNQSzZYd0NEWWJGelFodmZWNk82aXNERmtVRjJ1MHR1aV9ZM2ttV3lBTW12b2tjeTYwYV8xal9kN1F4TzR2VVRSWTA0TEN2eE91dkFmZWszMU1oMGw3TDB1WTh5UTNsMUZodGVWU2t4cDNHWnl3VHNHeUM1aG9hay0tRQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;NigerianEye&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikgFBVV95cUxOTFU3bUVsbmJWcllSRVlxMzhQUXQ5bVZsTTdVSk94R3piblgzdzJhUzRPT0dNMUYxaHJkMWVhcndqQk9lMzNnbnN3MkNkOVJYRmhMWjJlU3NfU211eGNuU18wM2RydW5weTNnSndoNkgwbGk3SG5Kd0J1YWh5ZUotb2ZpdUFGOWUxZDF2Q0pmOEJFUQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Trust&lt;/a